From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 22 Jun 2026 16:51:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03495/11362] [outer-loop] L2-findability diagnostic: L2 is
 GRADIENT-bound not budget-bound (self-play loop blocked)

Tested whether the value's efficiency (which frees budget) could let exploration find L2. At budget
12000 from L1-complete on lp85, NEITHER value NOR blind reaches L2. So L2 is gradient-bound, not
budget-bound -- freeing budget does not help find it. Also: the value's discrimination is WEAK on
lp85 (on 19.9 ~= far 20.4) -- a matching game (not positional) with only ~6 L1 positives; the
spatial net's strength was navigation.

CONCLUSION: the self-play deepening loop CANNOT bootstrap -- there is no findable L2 seed win (so no
L2 data to train an L2 value), and the L1 value does not transfer across the level boundary. The
verifier-as-Q-head is a strong PER-LEVEL efficiency tool (7.6x routing where the value discriminates
+ has data) but NOT a deepener; the deep/hard levels remain a gradient+data wall. The shippable win
is per-level routing: upgrade the conductor's linear LearnedVerifier (cannot route) with the
position-aware SpatialValueNet + tuned weight.

verdict: complete: value_q_head_no_L2_deepening_gradient_bound_not_budget_bound
